# Implementation Plan

## Approach

Two parallel tracks that touch different layers: (A) wire DartAdapter into the FCA attribute pipeline by implementing FcaAttributeSource and enriching `extract_language_attrs`, and (B) add flag extraction so Dart symbols get test/lifecycle/FFI flags that suppress dead-code false positives. Both follow the existing Rust adapter pattern exactly — same trait, same flag constants, same JSON merge strategy.

## Files

- **Modify**: `src/parser/dart.rs` (~lines 240-301, plus new function) — add `extract_flags` function, enhance `extract_language_attrs` with getter/setter/override/returns_future, wire flags into `collect_symbols`
- **Modify**: `src/parser/adapter.rs` (~lines 219-237) — implement `FcaAttributeSource` for DartAdapter, add `DART_EFFECT_PATTERNS`, override `as_fca_source`
- **Modify**: `tests/parse-dart-test.rs` — add tests for new attrs and flags

## Steps

### Step 1: Enhance `extract_language_attrs` in dart.rs

Add detection for `is_getter`, `is_setter`, `has_override`, and `returns_future` to the existing function.

For getters/setters, check `sig_node` kind. For `has_override`, walk annotation children of the declaration node. For `returns_future`, inspect the return type node in the signature.

```rust
// Inside the Function | Method match arm, after existing sig_node handling:

// Getter/setter detection from signature node kind
if let Some(sig) = sig_node {
    let inner = if sig.kind() == \"method_signature\" {
        let mut c = sig.walk();
        sig.children(&c).find(|n| is_dart_signature_node(n.kind())).unwrap_or(sig)
    } else { sig };

    if inner.kind() == \"getter_signature\" {
        attrs.insert(\"is_getter\".into(), true.into());
    }
    if inner.kind() == \"setter_signature\" {
        attrs.insert(\"is_setter\".into(), true.into());
    }
}

// After the match block (applies to all kinds):
// has_override — check for @override annotation
if has_annotation(node, \"override\") {
    attrs.insert(\"has_override\".into(), true.into());
}
```

For `returns_future`, inspect the return type in the function signature node:

```rust
// Inside Function | Method arm, check return type for Future/FutureOr
if let Some(sig) = sig_node {
    let inner = /* resolve through method_signature as above */;
    if let Some(ret_type) = inner.child_by_field_name(\"return_type\")
        .or_else(|| inner.child_by_field_name(\"type\"))
    {
        let type_text = ret_type.utf8_text(src).unwrap_or(\"\");
        if type_text.starts_with(\"Future\") || type_text.starts_with(\"FutureOr\") {
            attrs.insert(\"returns_future\".into(), true.into());
        }
    }
}
```

Note: the `_src` parameter in the current signature needs to be renamed to `src` (remove underscore prefix) since we'll now use it for `returns_future` text extraction.

